# Review is required for the things that decide behaviour, and for the front door.
#
# Manifests are here because "no new dependencies without a reason that survives scrutiny"
# is a rule nothing else enforces. deny.toml is here because it is where that rule's
# mechanical half is granted an exception: an ignored advisory, an allowed licence, a
# duplicate version nobody has to account for again.
#
# The rest is what decides what executes with this tree checked out, and who decides it: the
# workflows, the image the released binaries are built in, the script an install runs, the hook npm
# runs on install, the three pnpm lockfiles, and the three pnpm-workspace.yaml files, which list
# the dependencies trusted to run a script on install. None of these was owned, so the one approval
# the protection requires for a change that moves a pinned step onto a movable tag was owed to
# nobody in particular. required-checks.txt is here for the same reason: it is the tree's statement of
# which checks hold a merge.
#
# Last matching pattern wins, so keep the more specific rules below the general ones.

/README.md @bbondy

/Cargo.toml @bbondy
/crates/*/Cargo.toml @bbondy
/package.json @bbondy
/deny.toml @bbondy

/.github/workflows/ @bbondy
/.github/CODEOWNERS @bbondy
/Dockerfile.cross @bbondy
/install.sh @bbondy
/npm/scripts/ @bbondy
/ui/package.json @bbondy
/ui/pnpm-lock.yaml @bbondy
/docs/website/pnpm-lock.yaml @bbondy
/packages/agent-client/pnpm-lock.yaml @bbondy
/ui/pnpm-workspace.yaml @bbondy
/docs/website/pnpm-workspace.yaml @bbondy
/packages/agent-client/pnpm-workspace.yaml @bbondy
/Cargo.lock @bbondy
/contrib/required-checks.txt @bbondy
